 ### KVMem statistics extension
 
+For experimental single-GPU Qwen prefill, `NINFER_PREFILL_PAGE_LSE_REUSE=1`
+records the already-computed softmax tile weights for the existing sampled
+queries. On the D256, 24-query-head / 4-KV-head, plain FP8 cache prompt route
+used on Ada, adjacent tiles contribute to each 64-token logical page. Each head
+is normalized over the whole visible cache before averaging. Query selection,
+Mean-K granularity, KV budget and sampling cadence are unchanged. The capture
+uses the existing feedback scratch. Decode, Query replay, incompatible shapes,
+short-row routes and unsupported devices use the existing computation. Leave the
+variable unset for the reference page-statistics route. The prompt kernel rounds
+its rotated Q and decoded K to BF16: its page probabilities need not be bitwise
+equal to the reference FP32 dot-product statistics, especially near a ranking tie.
+
 KVMem's Qwen3.5-core dense path supports explicit heads tensor parallelism:
 `--devices 0,1 --tensor-parallel --tensor-attention heads`. Merely selecting two
 devices retains layer-pipeline placement. Optional `--tensor-split 3,1` weights
